· Multiplanetary validation: Detailed lunar/Martian case studies with mass budgets, reliability analyses, and ISRU pathways would test the universality claim.

Despite these limitations, the framework is fully falsifiable. An empirical test could construct a small‑scale FESA microgrid and compare its performance against a single‑technology baseline under identical demand and perturbation scenarios, measuring κ_exergy and failure probabilities.

